The optional legacy-hlsl feature includes HLSL translation and binding code in
src/hlsl.rs and src/hlsl/ derived from the TomBox contributors’ tuxbox-xshader
crate, via brcly/TomBox at ca6cf6a6b44e36d3ca4420db55a660a7bc6d6d5a plus
working-tree changes. The original crate is MIT OR Apache-2.0. This distribution
selects Apache-2.0. See ../../docs/licenses/tombox/Apache-2.0.txt.

Modified for TuxBox in November 2026, including wave operations, buffer and
texture addressing, compute programs and linked raster signatures. The
legacy-hlsl feature is enabled in the gameplay build.

The DXBC, PSV0, RTS0, XDAT, FSSM and FSPX readers, RDNA instruction decoder
and the pixel and compute emitters in constant_pixel.rs and compute_hlsl.rs were independently implemented for TuxBox.
The generated opcode names and assignments use AMD's machine-readable ISA
